@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07, the capstone: the monthly net income of an employed parent in 2026.
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else.
--
-- Every adapter (il07-adapter-il0N.l4) and the pipeline import this module. An
-- adapter imports this module and ONE row's modules, so each name below must be
-- distinct from every name in every row: that is why the types carry "IL-07"
-- and the fields name whose fact they are ("the earner's ...", "the spouse's
-- ..."). RECONCILE.md lists the rows' own clashing nouns.
--
-- Membership test (encoding-a-subject, step 4): a witness of ordinary
-- competence could testify to the fact, or a register, a payslip or a return
-- records it. Whether the fact makes tax or contributions payable, or an
-- allowance due, is a rule, and belongs to the row that encodes it.
--
-- Money is new Israeli shekels (NIS), as a bare NUMBER.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 — the household`

§§ `The earner`

-- INPUT CONVENTIONS (BRIEF.md, "The household"):
-- * `the earner's monthly salary` is the gross salary from one employer, income
--   from employment under ITO s 2(2) and so from personal exertion (ITO s 1).
-- * `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`: the
--   capstone apportions the year's tax to a month only on this footing (NOTES.md,
--   fork K1).
-- * The two residence facts are separate because the two Laws define residence
--   separately: ITO s 1 "תושב ישראל" (row IL-01 takes it as an input) and the
--   NII's "יושב בישראל" in s 65 (row IL-06 takes it as an input).
--   VERSION 0.3.0: the ITO fact is residence as the Ordinance treats it, s 3A(f)
--   included: an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area, or operates in
--   it, is treated "as if" an Israeli resident (ITO line 471), so the caller gives
--   TRUE. Row IL-01 v0.2.0 takes s 3A(f)'s two facts separately; the capstone
--   gives them as FALSE and lets this field carry them (il07-adapter-il01.l4).
-- * `the earner is a foreign worker` and `... the Area ...` are read only so that
--   row IL-01's refusals for ITO ss 48A and 48 are reached where they apply.
-- * `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the
--   earner`: Schedule K's minimum for an employee is the minimum wage applicable
--   to that employee (row IL-05, fork F11); the capstone holds only the full
--   adult figure the Institute publishes.
-- * `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 ...`: NII s 342(c)(2)'s age
--   for a woman, read from Schedule A1 Part D by month of birth (not encoded by
--   any row: row IL-05 takes it in months). NOTHING for a man.
--   SUPERSEDED IN PART by version 0.2.0: row IL-08 encodes Part D, and the
--   pipeline computes the age from the date of birth. NOTHING now means "not
--   given" and the computed age is used; a figure given must equal it, or the
--   deduction is declined.
-- * `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond
--   those the composed rows encode`: the rows encode the credit points of
--   ss 34, 36, 36A, s 37 as halved by s 66(c)(2), and s 66(c)'s children's
--   points. Every other credit and deduction (s 35 for a new immigrant, ss 39A
--   and 39B, ss 40A-40D, s 44, s 45, s 45A for life-insurance and pension
--   contributions, s 47 for provident-fund deposits, and the rest) lowers the
--   tax and is not encoded (GAPS.md). An employee with mandatory pension
--   contributions has a s 45A credit, so for most real employees this is FALSE,
--   and the capstone then declines rather than overstate the tax.
--   READ IN VERSION 0.2.0 AS: the earner has no credit or deduction beyond those
--   IL-07 computes from the household and its further facts (ss 34, 35, 36, 36A,
--   37-39, 40(b), 45A, 47 and 66(c)). A caller of version 0.1.0, who gives no
--   further facts, says by TRUE what it said before: no s 35, s 45A or s 47
--   credit or deduction, so the further facts it implies give none (pipeline,
--   `IL-07: no further facts`). TRUE also says the earner is in no class for
--   which regulations under ITO s 47(d) set higher deductions (row IL-08 does
--   not encode them). FALSE declines the tax, in either version.
DECLARE `IL-07 earner` HAS
    `the earner's name`                                                              IS A STRING
    `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS A DATE
    `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The spouse, and the couple's elections`

-- `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year`: the household has one earner;
-- a spouse with income is outside it (the pipeline declines, NOTES.md fork K4).
-- `the spouse is a housewife ...`: NII s 238 (source line 2428) defines
-- "עקרת בית" as a married woman, other than an agunah, whose spouse is insured
-- under Chapter 11 and who is neither an employee nor self-employed; row IL-06
-- takes the status as an input, and so does this row.
DECLARE `IL-07 spouse` HAS
    `the spouse's name`                                                              IS A STRING
    `the spouse is a woman`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the spouse is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse is a housewife as defined in section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- `the earner is the registered spouse`: ITO s 64B decides who is "בן הזוג
-- הרשום"; no row encodes it, so it is an input (as in row IL-02).
-- `the earner claims a separate calculation ...`: the election of ITO s 66(a)(1)
-- (the spouse who is not registered) and s 66(c)(1A) (either spouse); row IL-02
-- records both in one field of `A spouse`.
-- `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37`: ITO s 37 is
-- not encoded; row IL-02 takes the answer as an input and halves it under
-- s 66(c)(2).
-- SUPERSEDED IN PART by version 0.2.0: row IL-08 encodes ss 37-39, and the point
-- is taken from s 37 on the statuses it reads (`IL-07 the statuses section 37
-- reads`, below). This field must then agree with s 37's answer; TRUE without
-- the statuses is declined.
-- `the earner is the registered spouse`: row IL-08 encodes s 64B, but its rules
-- read the couple's incomes two years back and their elections, which the
-- household does not hold; who is registered stays an input (GAPS.md item 3).
DECLARE `IL-07 couple` HAS
    `the earner's spouse`                                                            IS AN `IL-07 spouse`
    `the earner is the registered spouse`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner claims a separate calculation of the tax on the earner's income from personal exertion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `A child of the household`

-- The earner's own child and, where there is a spouse, the spouse's too;
-- unmarried, in Israel, living with the parent or parents (BRIEF.md).
-- `the child's mother elects ...`: ITO s 66(c)(4)(a1), the mother's election to
-- count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year.
DECLARE `IL-07 child` HAS
    `the child's name`                                                               IS A STRING
    `the child's date of birth`                                                      IS A DATE
    `the child's mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The household in a month`

-- `the health insurance contribution the caller says is deducted for the month`:
-- health insurance contributions are imposed by the National Health Insurance
-- Law 5754-1994, which no row encodes (GAPS.md). The caller supplies the amount.
DECLARE `IL-07 household in a month` HAS
    `the year of the month`                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the month of the year`                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the earner`                                                                     IS AN `IL-07 earner`
    `the couple, if the earner has a spouse`                                         IS A MAYBE `IL-07 couple`
    `the children of the household`                                                  IS A LIST OF `IL-07 child`
    `the health insurance contribution the caller says is deducted for the month`    IS A NUMBER

§ `IL-07 — the further facts version 0.2.0 reads`

-- Version 0.2.0 (2026-10-07) composes row IL-08 as well (ITO ss 35, 37-39,
-- 40(b), 45A, 47, 65; NII s 72, s 335, Schedule A1 Part D). The household
-- records above are unchanged, so every caller of version 0.1.0, and the
-- independent tests (tests-independent.l4), are answered as before wherever no
-- provision now encoded changes the answer. The facts IL-08's sections read and
-- the household records do not hold are here, in one record the pipeline's
-- version 0.2.0 rules take as a second argument (`..., with further facts` f).
-- A caller of the version 0.1.0 rules gets `IL-07: no further facts`
-- (il07-pipeline.l4). Same membership test as above.

§§ `Sections 45A and 47: the earner's pension contributions and insurance`

-- `the earner's own contribution to a pension provident fund, each month`: the
--   employee's deposit deducted from the salary; s 45A(b) "sums he paid to a
--   pension provident fund", and the sums s 47(b) and (b1) deduct.
-- `the employer's deposits to a pension provident fund for the earner, each
--   month`: benefits and severance together. With the earner's own, they are the
--   sums "paid for him, in respect of his income" that make a beneficiary member
--   (s 47(a)(7); row IL-08's fork F2 counts every component).
-- `the part of the monthly salary that is insured income`: s 47(a)(4), work
--   income for which the employer paid to a pension fund; the payslip records it.
-- `paid in the tax year for ...`: s 45A(b)'s survivors' pension insurance and
--   (a)(1)'s life insurance, by the earner or the spouse, for the year.
-- A month's figures are the same in every month of the year (the salary is,
-- fork K1), so the year's are twelve times them.
DECLARE `IL-07 the earner's pension contributions and insurance` HAS
    `the earner's own contribution to a pension provident fund, each month`          IS A NUMBER
    `the employer's deposits to a pension provident fund for the earner, each month` IS A NUMBER
    `the part of the monthly salary that is insured income`                          IS A NUMBER
    `paid in the tax year for survivors' pension insurance`                          IS A NUMBER
    `paid in the tax year for insurance of the earner's or the spouse's life`        IS A NUMBER

§§ `Section 35: the earner's immigration`

-- ITO s 35(d) "עולה": the grounds row IL-08 encodes, in this row's own names (an
-- adapter maps them; RECONCILE.md). A returning resident carries the two facts
-- s 35(d) "תושב חוזר" reads.
DECLARE `IL-07 the ground on which the earner is an immigrant` IS ONE OF
    `IL-07: an immigrant's visa or certificate under the Law of Return`
    `IL-07: entitled to such a visa or certificate, with a visa or licence for temporary residence`
    `IL-07: a returning resident` HAS
        `the day the earner returned and became an Israeli resident`                 IS A DATE
        `the earner had been a foreign resident for six consecutive years before it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `IL-07: of a class the Minister of Finance has determined to be treated as an immigrant`
    `IL-07: none of the grounds of section 35(d)`

-- `it was the first time the earner became an immigrant`: s 35(c) "ולא יינתן
--   אלא בפעם הראשונה שנעשה לעולה".
-- `the Minister's rules under section 35(e) reach the earner`: the rules of
--   5738-1977, not in the source bundle (row IL-08 declines where they reach).
-- The months of the tax year the earner resided in Israel are not asked: the
-- household is not absent from Israel (BRIEF.md), so every month of the year is
-- given, and s 35 itself gives nothing for a month before the immigration.
DECLARE `IL-07 the earner's immigration` HAS
    `the ground of immigration`                                                      IS AN `IL-07 the ground on which the earner is an immigrant`
    `the earner's Israeli citizenship was cancelled under section 10(d) of the Citizenship Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the earner became an immigrant`                                         IS A DATE
    `it was the first time the earner became an immigrant`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister's rules under section 35(e) reach the earner`                      IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Section 37: the statuses it reads`

-- ITO s 37 "יחיד מוטב": the earner or the spouse past retirement age (the
-- Retirement Age Law, not in the bundle: a status), or blind or disabled within
-- s 9(5)(a) or (a1); and the assessing officer's finding that the spouse's
-- maintenance was on the earner. Read only where the earner has a spouse.
DECLARE `IL-07 the statuses section 37 reads` HAS
    `the earner has reached retirement age`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner's spouse has reached retirement age`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is blind or disabled within section 9(5)(a) or (a1)`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner's spouse is blind or disabled within section 9(5)(a) or (a1)`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner proved to the assessing officer that the spouse's maintenance was on the earner in the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Section 335 of the National Insurance Law: the earner's insurance statuses`

-- Each is another Chapter's answer, which the Institute records (row IL-08's
-- `A person in a contribution period, for section 335`). The two the household
-- already holds (resident in Israel, insured under Chapter 11) are the earner
-- record's; the earner is an employee, so never a housewife under s 238.
DECLARE `IL-07 the earner's insurance statuses, for section 335` HAS
    `the earner is insured under Chapter 5, work injury`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is insured under Chapter 6, accident injury`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is insured for unemployment, under paragraph (1) of insured in section 158` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is an employee insured under Chapter 8, insolvency`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is insured under Chapter 9, disability`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is insured for long-term care`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is a widow pensioner as defined in section 238`                      IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Section 40(b): a parent without a spouse, and the children's other parent`

-- One entry per child of the household, matched to the child by its name (so
-- every child needs a name of its own). The facts s 40(b)(1A) and (3) read about
-- the child's other parent.
DECLARE `IL-07 a child's other parent, for section 40(b)` HAS
    `the name of the child`                                                          IS A STRING
    `the child's other parent died in or before the tax year`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child is registered in the population register without the details of one parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child's other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child's other parent has credit points for the child under section 40(b)(1)`        IS A BOOLEAN

-- `the earner and the children are a single-parent family`: s 40(b)(1)
--   "הורה במשפחה חד־הורית" and (1A) "ילד במשפחה חד־הורית"; undefined in the
--   Ordinance (row IL-08, A5), a status. The household is one family, so the
--   earner's status and each child's are the same fact.
-- `the earner maintained the children in the tax year`: (1) "שכלכלתם היתה עליו".
-- `the earner lives apart from the children's other parent`, `the earner's share
--   of the children's maintenance expenses` (0 to 1): s 40(b)(2).
DECLARE `IL-07 the single-parent family, for section 40(b)` HAS
    `the earner and the children are a single-parent family`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner maintained the children in the tax year`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner lives apart from the children's other parent`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner's share of the children's maintenance expenses`                      IS A NUMBER
    `each child's other parent`                                                      IS A LIST OF `IL-07 a child's other parent, for section 40(b)`

§§ `The further facts, together`

-- `the earner's immigration, if the earner is an immigrant`: NOTHING for one who
--   is not.
-- `the statuses section 37 reads, if given`: NOTHING where not given; the
--   couple's s 37 field must then be FALSE, or the tax is declined.
-- `the earner's insurance statuses for section 335, if given`: NOTHING where not
--   given; an earner resident in Israel and insured under Chapter 11 is then
--   taken to be insured in every branch, as version 0.1.0 took every employee to
--   be (NOTES.md fork K16), and any other earner's contributions are declined.
-- `the single-parent family, if given`: read only where the earner has no
--   spouse and has children; NOTHING there declines the tax.
DECLARE `IL-07 further facts of the household` HAS
    `the earner's pension contributions and insurance`                               IS AN `IL-07 the earner's pension contributions and insurance`
    `the earner's immigration, if the earner is an immigrant`                        IS A MAYBE `IL-07 the earner's immigration`
    `the statuses section 37 reads, if given`                                        IS A MAYBE `IL-07 the statuses section 37 reads`
    `the earner's insurance statuses for section 335, if given`                      IS A MAYBE `IL-07 the earner's insurance statuses, for section 335`
    `the single-parent family, if given`                                             IS A MAYBE `IL-07 the single-parent family, for section 40(b)`

§ `IL-07 — what passes between the rows`

-- Schedule J's column D amount on the earner's wage, one field per branch for
-- which column D prints a figure. Row IL-04 computes each; row IL-05's s 342(c)
-- reads them. The two rows each declare their own `A branch of insurance`
-- (RECONCILE.md, clash N1), so the amounts cross between them in this record,
-- matched by the branch's name.
DECLARE `IL-07 column D amounts on the earner's wage` HAS
    `the column D amount for maternity`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the column D amount for accident injury`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `the column D amount for unemployment`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the column D amount for disability`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `the column D amount for long-term care`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `the column D amount for senior citizens and survivors`                          IS A NUMBER

-- The credit points ITO s 66(c) gives the earner, as row IL-02 counts them.
-- `... under section 36A, by paragraph (4)` is kept so that a test can compare
-- it with row IL-01's own s 36A half point; the pipeline counts s 36A once, from
-- row IL-01 (RECONCILE.md, clash N7).
DECLARE `IL-07 credit points section 66(c) gives the earner` HAS
    `IL-02's half point under section 36A, by section 66(c)(4)`                      IS A NUMBER
    `IL-02's half point under section 37, by section 66(c)(2)`                       IS A NUMBER
    `IL-02's points for children, by section 66(c)(4) to (6)`                        IS A NUMBER

-- NII s 335's answer for the earner, one field per branch. Rows IL-04, IL-05 and
-- IL-08 each declare their own `A branch of insurance` (RECONCILE.md, clash N1),
-- so the IL-08 adapter fills this record from IL-08's list and the IL-05 adapter
-- turns it into IL-05's, matched by the branch's name.
DECLARE `IL-07 branches in which contributions are payable for the earner` HAS
    `contributions are payable for maternity`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributions are payable for children`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributions are payable for work injury`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributions are payable for accident injury`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributions are payable for unemployment`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributions are payable for employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributions are payable for disability`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributions are payable for long-term care`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributions are payable for senior citizens and survivors`                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- ITO s 40(b)'s points for the earner, split as row IL-08 splits them.
DECLARE `IL-07 credit points under section 40(b)` HAS
    `points set against the tax generally, under section 40(b)(1) and (2)`           IS A NUMBER
    `points set against the tax on income from personal exertion, under section 40(b)(1A) and (1B)` IS A NUMBER

-- Which calculation governs the earner's tax for the year.
DECLARE `IL-07 the calculation of the earner's tax` IS ONE OF
    `an individual without a spouse`
    `a separate calculation under section 66`
    `the consolidated calculation under section 65, in the earner's name`

-- THE SCHEDULE J SWITCH (NOTES.md fork K14; RECONCILE.md R1 and section 5).
-- Above the reduced collection threshold, Schedule J column D's items for the six
-- deduction branches sum to 4.67 for 2026 and its totals row prints 7.00, the
-- rate the Institute deducts (row IL-04's open fork F4, which computes from the
-- items). Ruled by Meng, 2026-10-07: the printed totals by default, the items
-- kept as the alternative. The pipeline's rule `IL-07: the reading of Schedule J
-- column D the capstone takes` names the one in force.
DECLARE `IL-07 a reading of Schedule J column D above the reduced collection threshold` IS ONE OF
    `the sum of the items of the six deduction branches`
    `the printed total of column D`

-- VERSION 0.5.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-54). THE COMPOSED ROWS' FORKS THAT REACH
-- THE CAPSTONE'S ANSWER. Meng ruled on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG) that where the text is
-- silent each row has one named switch per fork, declined by default where the
-- readings part. Five such forks reach a household the capstone answers
-- (NOTES.md section 14). The capstone passes each on, by default at the row's own
-- switch, and lets a caller name a reading instead, so that a test whose author
-- decided a reading can ask it by name. Each type's first member is the default;
-- the others are the rows' readings, under names of this row (a row's own
-- constructor reaches every module that imports its adapter, so the names must
-- differ). Two defaults are the capstone's (fork K23): the set-off of the
-- children's credit and the further point of s 40(b) are each asked at both of
-- their row's readings and declined only where the tax differs, as fork K22 asks
-- s 72 at both readings of a missing day.

-- Rows IL-01 (fork F1, s 36A) and IL-02 (fork F20, s 66(c)(4)'s half point under
-- s 36A): does s 36A require the woman to be an Israeli resident? One question,
-- asked of both rows alike.
DECLARE `IL-07 a reading of section 36A on residence` IS ONE OF
    `IL-07: section 36A at the rows' own switches, declined where residence decides it`
    `IL-07: section 36A without a residence condition`
    `IL-07: section 36A only for an Israeli resident`

-- Row IL-02, fork F18: may the registered spouse request a separate calculation
-- under s 66(c)(1A)?
DECLARE `IL-07 a reading of section 66(c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS ONE OF
    `IL-07: section 66(c)(1A) at row IL-02's switch, declined where the readings differ`
    `IL-07: the registered spouse may request a separate calculation under section 66(c)(1A)`
    `IL-07: only the spouse who is not the registered spouse may request under section 66(c)(1A)`

-- Row IL-02, fork F13: is the children's credit under s 66(c)(4)-(5) capped at
-- the tax on income from personal exertion, or only set against it first?
DECLARE `IL-07 a reading of the set-off of the children's credit under section 66(c)(4)-(5)` IS ONE OF
    `IL-07: the children's credit under section 66(c), declined where its reading changes the tax`
    `IL-07: the children's credit capped at the tax on income from personal exertion`
    `IL-07: the children's credit set first against the tax on income from personal exertion`

-- Row IL-08 (income tax), fork F16: is the one further point of s 40(b)(1B) and
-- (2) given once, or once for each child?
DECLARE `IL-07 a reading of the further point under section 40(b)(1B) and (2)` IS ONE OF
    `IL-07: the further point under section 40(b), declined where its reading changes the tax`
    `IL-07: one further point under section 40(b)(1B) and (2), once`
    `IL-07: one further point under section 40(b)(1B) and (2), for each child`

-- Row IL-06, fork F6: is a child whose insured parent s 66 excludes still in
-- that parent's count under s 67(b)?
DECLARE `IL-07 a reading of the count of a parent excluded by section 66` IS ONE OF
    `IL-07: the count of an excluded parent at row IL-06's switch, declined where the readings differ`
    `IL-07: the child stays in the count of the parent section 66 excludes`
    `IL-07: the child goes to the count of another insured parent, not excluded`

-- VERSION 0.6.0 (BACKLOG IL-55). The full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged
-- 18 or over on the first day of each quarter of a year (row IL-32), which the IL-05
-- adapter passes to Schedule K item 1 (row IL-05) and fork K21 reads as its bound.
DECLARE `IL-07 the full monthly minimum wage of an adult on the first day of each quarter` HAS
    `on 1 January`                                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `on 1 April`                                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `on 1 July`                                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `on 1 October`                                                                   IS A NUMBER

-- VERSION 0.6.0 (BACKLOG IL-55). FACTS A CALLER MAY ADD, to reach a row the
-- capstone composes only on request. The household and its further facts are as
-- they were, so no caller's builder changes; a caller who has these facts names
-- them in the readings record below (its last field), and every rule that takes
-- that record sees them. `IL-07: no facts added` gives none, and every answer is
-- then version 0.5.0's.
--
-- Row IL-28 (ITO ss 48 and 48A, the Area order of 5755-1995 and the foreign worker
-- Regulations of 5775-2014): the facts it reads that the household does not hold.
-- The household holds whether the earner is a foreign worker within s 48A and
-- whether a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen; these are the rest.
DECLARE `IL-07 the earner's facts under sections 48 and 48A of the Income Tax Ordinance` HAS
    -- s 3A(a), which s 48 adopts: an Israeli citizen, and one entitled to immigrate
    -- under the Law of Return, is not reached by the Order.
    `the earner is an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- The months of the tax year in which the earner was a resident of the Area,
    -- NOTHING for the whole year.
    `the months of the tax year in which the earner was a resident of the Area, if not the whole year` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    -- REG 1, 2 and 3 of the Regulations, and the Foreign Workers Law s 1.
    `the earner is a resident of Israel within the Foreign Workers Law`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner holds a visa under section 2 of the Entry into Israel Law, or needs one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner's stay in Israel or the Area and employment there are permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner is an expert from abroad or a guest lecturer`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner holds a B/1 temporary worker visa and licence`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner holds a permit to work in the caring sector`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earner's stay is extended under section 3A(b) of the Entry into Israel Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the months of the tax year the earner spent in Israel or the Area`              IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `IL-07 the facts a caller adds` HAS
    `the earner's facts under sections 48 and 48A of the Income Tax Ordinance, if given` IS A MAYBE `IL-07 the earner's facts under sections 48 and 48A of the Income Tax Ordinance`

DECLARE `IL-07 the readings of the composed rows' forks` HAS
    `section 36A on residence (row IL-01 fork F1, row IL-02 fork F20)`                       IS AN `IL-07 a reading of section 36A on residence`
    `section 66(c)(1A) as to the registered spouse (row IL-02 fork F18)`                      IS AN `IL-07 a reading of section 66(c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`
    `the set-off of the children's credit under section 66(c)(4)-(5) (row IL-02 fork F13)`    IS AN `IL-07 a reading of the set-off of the children's credit under section 66(c)(4)-(5)`
    `the further point under section 40(b)(1B) and (2) (row IL-08 fork F16)`                 IS AN `IL-07 a reading of the further point under section 40(b)(1B) and (2)`
    `the count of a parent excluded by section 66 (row IL-06 fork F6)`                       IS AN `IL-07 a reading of the count of a parent excluded by section 66`
    -- Version 0.6.0: the facts a caller adds (above).
    `the facts a caller adds (version 0.6.0)`                                              IS AN `IL-07 the facts a caller adds`

§ `IL-07 — the answer`

-- The income tax for the tax year, with the figures it is made of. The fields
-- from `the calculation` on were added in version 0.2.0; each is 0 where its
-- section gives nothing or the calculation does not reach it.
DECLARE `IL-07 income tax for the tax year` HAS
    `the earner's taxable income in the tax year`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the tax under section 121`                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `the additional tax under section 121B`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the value of one credit point in the tax year`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A`                                IS A NUMBER
    `the half point under section 37, by section 66(c)(2)`                           IS A NUMBER
    `the credit points for children under section 66(c)`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the credit for children, set against the tax on income from personal exertion`  IS A NUMBER
    `the income tax for the tax year`                                                IS A NUMBER
    `the calculation`                                                                IS AN `IL-07 the calculation of the earner's tax`
    `the credit points under section 35`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39, in a consolidated calculation`  IS A NUMBER
    `the credit points for children under section 40(b)`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the credit under section 45A`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the deduction under section 47`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    -- Version 0.6.0: row IL-36's exemption, taken off the taxable income (fork K24).
    `the income exempt under the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `IL-07 the household's month` HAS
    `the gross salary for the month`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the income tax worked for the tax year`                                         IS AN `IL-07 income tax for the tax year`
    `one twelfth of the income tax for the tax year`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the national insurance contributions deducted from the salary for the month`    IS A NUMBER
    `the health insurance contribution deducted for the month`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the child allowance for the month`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the net income of the household for the month`                                  IS A NUMBER
